  - "eRegulations' platform.php=8.2 pin is the right modern PHP target"
  - "Modern cross-platform .NET tools target net6-8; SDK 8.0 LTS is an acceptable default"
deviations_from_plan: >
  "Scope broadened from strict macOS<->Ubuntu parity to 'ready-to-work machine,'
  per explicit user direction, which legitimizes macOS-only rows. Installer support
  for jvm/php/.NET/ios is follow-on work (topic installers + Brewfile); Xcode in
  particular is only partly scriptable (Mac App Store / xcode-select)."
trade_offs: >
  "Included .NET SDK as an opt-in row rather than omitting it (analyst flagged it
  niche) to honor 'ready to work' while signaling it's not default. iOS rows use
  n/a for Ubuntu rather than forcing a two-column fit. Version granularity stays
  'major' here; exact pins (Fastlane/CocoaPods/JDK) land at the installer layer."
self_review:
